KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 9 two-element fold in trailing decltype: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold] in a trailing-return-type decltype with a
pack instantiated at size >= 2.  Reducing the fold in typecheck_type
would need the replicated `<base>$k` value parameters, which are only
created during the called specialization's own body instantiation and
are not in scope while the trailing return type is checked.  CBMC
drops the whole declaration ("found no match for symbol 'sum'").  The
size-0/1 cases are fixed (see cpp17_fold_in_trailing_decltype);
accepted by g++/clang -std=c++17.
